# IRON NEST: Heavy Turret Simulator  (Steam appid 2950790)
#
# The first 64-bit D3D11 title in this environment. Everything the workbench has
# debugged so far was either 64-bit Chromium (Steam itself) or a 32-bit SDL 1.2
# game, so this exercises a code path -- wined3d's D3D11 -> Vulkan -> MoltenVK
# -> Metal chain -- that nothing here has touched.
#
# What it is, measured from the installed files rather than the store page:
#
#   engine        Unity 6 (6000.3.9f1), IL2CPP (GameAssembly.dll, no Mono)
#   exe           PE32+ x86_64, subsystem GUI -- no 32-bit build exists
#   graphics      D3D11 per PCGamingWiki; the build also ships D3D12/D3D12Core.dll
#                 (the Agility SDK), so D3D12 is compiled in and the runtime
#                 choice has to be read from the game's own Player.log
#   audio         FMOD Studio + Resonance Audio -- WASAPI/mmdevapi, NOT dsound,
#                 so the x87 mixer story (docs/NOTEBOOK.md) cannot apply here
#   anti-cheat    none
#   controllers   advertised as full support; irrelevant until the winebus/SDL2
#                 crash in RUNTIME.md section 1 is fixed. Keyboard/mouse only.
#
# Installed into the shared library on S:, so a per-game prefix later costs
# nothing.

RUNTIME="winecx-26.3.0-sse-x86_64"
PREFIX="steam-winecx"

# DXMT is REQUIRED here, not an optimisation. Measured 2026-08-14:
#
#   BACKEND="none"        wined3d -> Vulkan -> MoltenVK, capped at feature
#                         level 9_3, so D3D11 device creation returns E_FAIL and
#                         the game shows "Failed to initialize graphics".
#   BACKEND="dxmt-0.80-winecx-26.3.0-sse"   Direct3D 11.0 [level 11.1], reaches the main menu.
#
# The cap is not this game's fault and not fixable in wined3d: MoltenVK reports
# geometryShader / pipelineStatisticsQuery / shaderCullDistance = false, and
# adapter_vk.c's feature_level_10_supported() requires all three. Metal has no
# geometry-shader stage, so that will not change. See docs/NOTEBOOK.md.
#
# ⚠️ AND THIS LINE IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN. BACKEND= exports WINEDLLOVERRIDES,
# which is inherited down a process tree -- but this profile launches
# `steam.exe -applaunch`, so the game's real parent is the Steam client, whose
# own profile sets BACKEND="none". The override never reaches the game and it
# comes up on wined3d, i.e. it does not come up at all. The backend is selected
# for real by a per-application registry key, which is keyed on the exe and so
# survives any launch path:
#
#   bin/backend-install dxmt-0.80-winecx-26.3.0-sse steam-winecx \
#       winecx-26.3.0-sse-x86_64 --app 'Iron Nest Heavy Turret Simulator.exe'
#
# Kept here anyway because it is what a *direct* launch uses, and because the
# profile should still say which backend this game wants. See docs/RUNTIME.md
# section 9, "BACKEND= in a profile does NOT reach a Steam-launched game".
BACKEND="dxmt-0.80-winecx-26.3.0-sse"

# Launch through Steam, not the exe directly. Same reasoning as
# strategic-command.env: steam_api64.dll re-launches via steam://run/<appid>
# when the client is not already up, and that hand-off goes through Wine's URL
# handler, which does not inherit our environment.
EXE='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steam.exe'
WORKDIR="$PREFIXES_DIR/steam-winecx/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Steam"

ARGS="-applaunch 2950790"

# Default-through so a trace can be requested per run:
#   WINEDEBUG=+loaddll bin/gamerun iron-nest
PROFILE_ENV=(
    "WINEDEBUG=${WINEDEBUG--all}"
)

WINEDLLOVERRIDES=""
